      "description": "Class 5a: int(1/x,x,0,1) via menu-insertion (2nd+CLEAR opens menu, DOWN x2 selects 'int( definite' at ui.c:970, ENTER inserts). Expect either STATE_ERROR or the CECIDF 'Integral DIVERGES' result screen (src/split/processor.c handle_integral). Both are acceptable graceful outcomes; the CRC baseline captures whichever CalcEngine produces \u2014 but it must not crash to RAM Cleared.",
      "start": "vram_start",
      "size": "vram_16_size",
      "expected_CRCs": [
        "32BFD188"
      ],
      "timeout": 5000
    },
    "nonconv_dne_limit": {
      "description": "Class 5b: lim(1/x,x,0) via menu-insertion (DOWN x3 to ui.c:971 'lim('). Expect either the STATE_RESULT screen '= DNE (does not exist)' (processor.c:492) or a STATE_ERROR; both are graceful. CRC baseline captures actual behavior.",
      "start": "vram_start",
      "size": "vram_16_size",
      "expected_CRCs": [
        "32BFD188"
      ],
      "timeout": 5000
    },
    "oversize_taylor_100": {
      "description": "Class 6: taylor(sin(x),x,0,100) via menu-insertion (DOWN x6 to ui.c:974 'taylor('). Expect STATE_ERROR with 'Result too large' (OVERFLOW path, src/main.c:2324) or a bounded-term graceful failure. MUST NOT exhaust the 512-node pool and crash.",
      "start": "vram_start",
      "size": "vram_16_size",
      "expected_CRCs": [
        "B9B5D5E0"
      ],
      "timeout": 10000
    },
    "break_after_on_key": {
      "description": "Class 7: taylor(e^(x),x,0,50) \u2014 a deliberately slow computation \u2014 launched via menu, then ON pressed ~600ms into ENTER dispatch to trigger check_cancel() (runtime_globals.c). Expect the Cancelled path (src/main.c:2313) to return to STATE_INPUT with the expression intact. LCD should show the input screen, NOT an error and NOT a hang. CRC baseline captures the input state.",
      "start": "vram_start",
      "size": "vram_16_size",
